# A boundary is measured, never assumed.
#
# This kit asserts that `render` is BYTE-REPRODUCIBLE. Git's autocrlf would rewrite
# line endings on the way in and out, so the bytes a host committed and the bytes a
# host renders could differ while every participant behaved correctly — the claim
# would go on reading as true from inside. The reproducibility test would still pass
# locally and the guarantee would be false everywhere else.
#
# Therefore every text file in this repository is LF on disk and LF in the object
# store, on every platform, regardless of any local `core.autocrlf`.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
